    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5dbaa1bf",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: white trash; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a recycling bag filled with paper waste attached to a bicycle, with the text 'white trash' at the top and 'you are doing it right' at the bottom. The overall intent is to mock or demean individuals labeled as 'white trash' by sarcastically praising their recycling efforts. This is a harmful meme because it uses a derogatory racial slur ('white trash') to target a specific group, implying that their behavior (recycling) is somehow 'right' or 'acceptable' only because they are considered 'trash.' The juxtaposition of the text with the image creates a tone of ridicule and reinforces negative stereotypes about people from lower socioeconomic backgrounds, potentially causing emotional harm or reinforcing prejudice against them. The meme does not contain direct abusive, cyberbullying, or propaganda elements, but it is harmful due to its use of a derogatory term and its implication that the targeted group is inherently 'trash' despite their positive action (recycling).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6267a044"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
